      en: "Elephant Marsh, a vast wetland in southern Malawi, spans 1,200 km² and was declared a Ramsar site in 2016. It supports over 100 bird species and is a breeding ground for fish. The marsh provides livelihoods through fishing and farming, but faces threats from encroachment. Conservation efforts focus on sustainable use and flood mitigation.",
